From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 02:05:03 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 124/127] render: a full-screen layer covers the screen
 whatever the camera's zoom

A full-screen layer (models/util/fullscreenlayer.json) drew its last pass through the scene's view, zoom and camera
position included. 3042492564's camera object zooms 0.73: its full-screen `localcontrast` layer drew the effect's
output into the zoomed 73 % rectangle (x 259-1660, y 146-886 at 1920), a copy of the whole frame shrunk into it, so a
lighter rectangle sat over the sea and sky even with the effect at strength 0. The layer now draws with the view
without the frame's adjustment, as a 3D scene's screen layers already do (getScreenProjection).

Measured in WE (private copies: the background and the layer, the camera kept): at strength 3 WE's effect changes
pixels across the whole frame (x 0-1919), at strength 0 none; ours changed only the rectangle at both. Now: x 0-1919
at strength 3, nothing at strength 0; mean |WE - ours| 3.70 -> 1.65 (strength 3), 3.39 -> 0.79 (strength 0, the
copy without the layer 0.79). Host test fullscreen_layer_ignores_zoom (corner blue unpatched, red patched).

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/reports/scene-we-ref.md (3042492564: the lighter rectangle; ~/.cache/liascape/we-ref/captures/var/v3042-bg*)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Vg3T4kWN88ooeafgoHLbfM
---
 src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Camera.cpp         |  2 ++
 src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Camera.h           |  3 +++
 src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Objects/CImage.cpp | 11 +++++++++--
 3 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Camera.cpp b/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Camera.cpp
index 4087124..768e74f 100644
--- a/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Camera.cpp
+++ b/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Camera.cpp
@@ -29,6 +29,8 @@ const glm::mat4& Camera::getProjection () const { return this->m_projection; }
 
 const glm::mat4& Camera::getLookAt () const { return this->m_view; }
 
+const glm::mat4& Camera::getUnadjustedLookAt () const { return this->m_lookat; }
+
 void Camera::setViewAdjust (const glm::mat4& adjust) {
     this->m_adjust = adjust;
     this->m_view = this->m_lookat * adjust;
diff --git a/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Camera.h b/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Camera.h
index b3391d1..f80790b 100644
--- a/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Camera.h
+++ b/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Camera.h
@@ -54,6 +54,9 @@ public:
     [[nodiscard]] const glm::mat4& getProjection () const;
     /** The view: the lookAt with the frame's adjustment (zoom, camera shake) applied in world space */
     [[nodiscard]] const glm::mat4& getLookAt () const;
+    /** The view without the frame's adjustment: where a full-screen layer draws (it covers the screen whatever the
+     *  zoom, shake or camera position) */
+    [[nodiscard]] const glm::mat4& getUnadjustedLookAt () const;
     /** Sets the frame's world-space view adjustment (CScene::updateCamera) */
     void setViewAdjust (const glm::mat4& adjust);
     /**
diff --git a/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Objects/CImage.cpp b/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Objects/CImage.cpp
index d9091d0..4e2de23 100644
--- a/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Objects/CImage.cpp
+++ b/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Objects/CImage.cpp
@@ -2132,8 +2132,15 @@ bool CImage::isPerspectiveLayer () const {
 glm::mat4 CImage::screenViewProjection () const {
     const auto& camera = this->getScene ().getCamera ();
 
-    // a 3D scene's screen layers keep the 2D layout over the scene's target
-    return camera.isPerspective () ? camera.getScreenProjection () : camera.getProjection () * camera.getLookAt ();
+    // a 3D scene's screen layers keep the 2D layout over the scene's target. A full-screen layer covers the target
+    // whatever the camera's zoom, shake and position: measured in WE on 3042492564 (its camera's zoom 0.73, a private
+    // copy with its `localcontrast` layer at strength 3), the effect changes pixels across the whole frame and at
+    // strength 0 none; ours drew its output into the zoomed 73 % rectangle, the frame shrunk into it
+    if (camera.isPerspective ()) {
+	return camera.getScreenProjection ();
+    }
+    return camera.getProjection ()
+	* (this->getImage ().model->fullscreen ? camera.getUnadjustedLookAt () : camera.getLookAt ());
 }
 
 void CImage::updateWorldPosition () {
